  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is trying to buy some items from a store, and then resell them elsewhere to make a profit. For the iii-th item, Chef knows that he can resell it for AiA_iAi​ coins.\n\nThe store has an ongoing offer. The first KKK items that Chef buys will be offered at a discount of 555 coins each, but the remaining items will all be offered at 101010 coins each.\n\nChef can choose to buy any number of items, and in any order that he desires. What is the maximum profit Chef can make?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum profit.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤K≤N≤1001 \\le K \\le N \\le 1001≤K≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤151 \\le A_i \\le 151≤Ai​≤15"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n2 1\n15 15\n2 1\n6 10\n2 2\n6 10\n5 3\n10 12 3 6 7\n2 2\n1 1",
        "output": "15\n5\n6\n14\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: Chef bought the first item for cost of 555 and resold it for 151515 coins. Then, he buys the second item for cost of 101010 and resold it for 151515. His total profit is 15−5+15−10=1515 - 5 + 15 - 10 = 1515−5+15−10=15 coins.\nTest Case 2: Chef bought the second item for cost of 555 and resold it for 101010 coins. The total profit is 555 coins."
      }
    ]
  },
